# docs/images is 45% of the engine module by size and is documentation, not
# code. Excluding it from the archive keeps `go get` from downloading README
# screenshots, while `git clone` still gets them and GitHub still renders them.
#
# This works because cmd/go builds module zips with `git archive`, which honours
# export-ignore from the tree being archived. Note "from the tree": an
# uncommitted .gitattributes has no effect, which makes the obvious test of this
# report no change at all.
docs/images/** export-ignore

# miniaudio.h is 4.1 MB of vendored third-party C -- more than three times the
# size of every Go file in the repo -- so Linguist counts the whole engine as a
# C project. Marking it vendored keeps it out of the language stats without
# hiding it from diffs or search.
audio/miniaudio.c linguist-vendored
audio/miniaudio.h linguist-vendored

# The .inc files are GLSL fragments pulled in by #include, not C++. Linguist
# maps the .inc extension to C++ by default, which put a C++ slice on the
# language bar for code that no C++ compiler has ever seen.
shaders/*.inc linguist-language=GLSL
